From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: michael moore <mrmoore27@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 08:49:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/27] wire: a BIP322 verifier for the registration's payout
 binding

Simple and full formats for P2WPKH, P2TR key path, P2WSH (single key and bare multisig),
P2SH-P2WPKH, P2SH-P2WSH, P2SH multisig and P2PKH, under standard BIP143/BIP341/legacy
sighash. Anything else (taproot script paths that commit, timelock scripts, proof of funds)
is inconclusive, which the BIP allows a verifier without an interpreter to say; it is never
accepted. SIGHASH_ALL|SIGHASH_UNIFIED (0x21) is checked under Knots' UnifiedSighash only
with the unified-sighash feature: XBT Knots wallets sign with it by default.

Tested against the official BIP322 vectors (basic and generated) and against XBT vectors
signed by XBT Knots wallets on regtest, standard and unified.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
